What's new (Tue Sep 29 22:35:18 MSK 2026):
*) A simple script for Mikrotik has been added to automatically update the system, with control over the version being installed.

What's new (Fri Oct  2 18:37:58 MSK 2026):
*) cron added
*) The comments in the scripts for MikroTik are written in English.
*) A local cache of responses from MikroTik servers has been added.

What's new (Fri Oct  9 20:31:36 MSK 2026):
*) Model and serial number are now checked by force_update.php to decide whether the update is allowed.
*) Device script: fixed removal of old backups, existing script is deleted before re-import, comments translated to English.

What's new (Sun Oct 11 22:36:08 MSK 2026):
*) Script variants without an explicit update channel added (the channel currently set on the device is used).

What's new (Tue Oct 13 17:28:08 MSK 2026):
*) The version caching algorithm has been changed: a cache hit is now final (upstream is not queried), the timestamp in the cache line is informational only; the 3-hour TTL was dropped.
*) ros-warmup.pl added: after every sync it re-requests the newest WARMUP_KEEP versions per endpoint so devices never trigger the first upstream lookup.
*) Synchronisation scripts now log to syslog only (logger, daemon facility); LOG_DIR / file logging and addons/get_6_upgrade_list.sh have been removed.
*) Default mirror path changed from /mnt/md0/mirror/routeros to /var/www/html/routeros.
*) PHP endpoints moved to html/mt-proxy/, seed cache files to html/routeros/. Parameters live in mt_proxy_config.php, update rules in mt_proxy_rules.php, cache file paths are derived from DOCUMENT_ROOT.
*) nginx configuration reworked (mt-fastcgi.conf snippet), Apache site configuration fixed.

What's new (Wed Oct 14 22:08:21 MSK 2026):
*) Web admin added (html/mt-proxy/index.php + db.php, SQLite with WAL): auto-registered devices, per-serial and per-model allowed-version lists, global version list, search, bulk edit.
*) force_update.php now stores device inventory (serial, model, IPs, currentFirmware/upgradeFirmware, last offered version) in mt_proxy.db; the decision chain is device list -> model rule -> global versions -> mt_proxy_rules.php (migration only) -> allowed_versions_hardcoded.
*) Device scripts replaced by BackupAndUpdate / BKPUPD-UPDATER / install_updater (https and -http variants), self-updating via BackupAndUpdate.md5, reboot-loop protection with failure counters.
*) Apache configuration split into conf-available/php-autodetect.conf (FPM or mod_php auto-detection) and sites-available/00-mirror.conf; html/fullchain.pem certificate bundle added; dns.rsc added.

What's new (Thu Oct 15 10:54:14 MSK 2026):
*) shell/Perl scripts moved into scripts/.
*) Apache: php-autodetect and 00-mirror.conf corrected; the -http variants now ship as ready .rsc files (install_updater-http.rsc, BackupAndUpdate-http.rsc, BKPUPD-UPDATER-http.rsc).
*) BackupAndUpdate.md5 and addons/mikrotik/readme*.md removed - keep the checksum generated on the mirror, the device scripts are documented in the main README now.
*) nginx site.conf updated to match the Apache routing.

